From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:05:30 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] qwen3_5: an MTP hold prices as a fixed cost of a
 drafted greedy shared round (TF_MTP_FIXED_HOLD)

Shared prices fit a drafted round's excess over the plain point as a per-row slope. An MTP hold costs
about the same however few drafts it holds, so few rows made the slope steep, the allocator cut drafts,
and the next fit was steeper: 8 short greedy chats settled 11-17% below plain decode after the first wave.
With hold_fixed, every drafting greedy round's extra rows and residual feed a decayed least-squares fit:
its intercept is a fixed cost of any drafting round (the hold), its slope what a row costs past the
forward table at this context. Until the rounds' extra rows spread enough to separate the two (a
variance of 4 rows squared), the per-row price stands. Sampled rounds keep the per-row price: on mixed
sampled traffic the fit drafted about half as much and served 7-13% fewer requests. Off by default
(Model.hold_fixed).
